Clouds reflected in Osawa Pond at Daikaku-ji Temple, and cherry leaves turning red.
</p>
<p class="jp">
大覚寺の大沢池に映る雲と、赤く色づいた桜の葉。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Arashiyama" /><category term="Ponds" /><category term="Daikaku-ji" /><category term="Clouds" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Clouds reflected in Osawa Pond at Daikaku-ji Temple, and cherry leaves turning red. 大覚寺の大沢池に映る雲と、赤く色づいた桜の葉。]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100471.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100471.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry><entry><title type="html">Japanese Garden・日本庭園</title><link href="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261028/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Japanese Garden・日本庭園" /><published>2026-10-28T00:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-28T00:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://hermosawavephotography.com/okazaki-garden</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261028/"><![CDATA[<p class="en">
Clouds reflect in the pond of the Japanese Garden, at the Kyoto City Kyocera Museum of Art.
</p>
<p class="jp">
京都市京セラ美術館の日本庭園にある池に、雲が映っている。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Higashiyama" /><category term="Gardens" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Clouds reflect in the pond of the Japanese Garden, at the Kyoto City Kyocera Museum of Art. 京都市京セラ美術館の日本庭園にある池に、雲が映っている。]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100445_edit.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100445_edit.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry><entry><title type="html">Morning on the Oi River・大堰川の朝</title><link href="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261023/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Morning on the Oi River・大堰川の朝" /><published>2026-10-23T00:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-23T00:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://hermosawavephotography.com/morning</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261023/"><![CDATA[<p class="en">
Early morning, looking west from the Togetsukyo Bridge. The autumn leaves are just beginning to turn.
</p>
<p class="jp">
早朝、渡月橋から西を眺めた。紅葉がちょうど色づき始めたところだ。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Arashiyama" /><category term="Dawn" /><category term="Togetsu Bridge" /><category term="Mountains" /><category term="Katsura River" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Early morning, looking west from the Togetsukyo Bridge. The autumn leaves are just beginning to turn. 早朝、渡月橋から西を眺めた。紅葉がちょうど色づき始めたところだ。]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100416.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100416.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry><entry><title type="html">Red Dawn・レッドドーン</title><link href="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261022/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Red Dawn・レッドドーン" /><published>2026-10-22T00:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-22T00:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://hermosawavephotography.com/dawn</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261022/"><![CDATA[<p class="en">
Red clouds at dawn, along the Katsura River in Arashiyama.
</p>
<p class="jp">
嵐山の桂川沿いで、夜明けの茜色の雲。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Arashiyama" /><category term="Dawn" /><category term="Togetsu Bridge" /><category term="Katsura River" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Red clouds at dawn, along the Katsura River in Arashiyama. 嵐山の桂川沿いで、夜明けの茜色の雲。]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100389.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100389.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry><entry><title type="html">Moss Garden・苔園</title><link href="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261019/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Moss Garden・苔園" /><published>2026-10-19T00:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-19T00:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://hermosawavephotography.com/moss-garden</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261019/"><![CDATA[<p class="en">
The garden in front of the <em>Tekisuian</em> tea house at Okochi Sanso, in the hills of Arashiyama.
</p>
<p class="jp">
嵐山の丘に建つ大河内山荘、茶室「適水庵」の前に広がる苔庭。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Arashiyama" /><category term="Gardens" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The garden in front of the Tekisuian tea house at Okochi Sanso, in the hills of Arashiyama. 嵐山の丘に建つ大河内山荘、茶室「適水庵」の前に広がる苔庭。]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100303.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100303.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry><entry><title type="html">Saigu Gyoretsu・斎宮行列</title><link href="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261018/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Saigu Gyoretsu・斎宮行列" /><published>2026-10-18T00:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-18T00:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://hermosawavephotography.com/saigu</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261018/"><![CDATA[<p class="en">
Each year, Nonomiya Shrine hosts a reenactment of the departure of the Saigu, an unmarried imperial princess sent to serve as high priestess at the Grand Shrine of Ise (Ise Jingu). The tradition dates to the Heian era. Here, the Saigu has stepped down from her palanquin and is making her way to the river for purification rituals.
</p>
<p class="en">

 <a href="https://www.discoverkyoto.com/event-calendar/october/saigu-gyoretsu-arashiyama/" target="_blank">More about this historical reenactment...</a>

</p>
<p class="jp">
野宮神社では毎年、平安時代に皇女（内親王）が斎宮として選ばれ、伊勢神宮へ旅立った様子を再現しています。この写真では、斎宮が輿から降り、川での禊の儀式に向かうところです。
</p>
<p class="jp">
    <a href="https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E6%96%8E%E5%AE%AE%E8%A1%8C%E5%88%97" target="_blank">この歴史再現イベントの詳細については……</a>
</p>

